  "description": "The Drupal breakpoints for the project are stored under **themes/custom/mytheme/config/breakpoints**, and they belong to the **mytheme** theme.\n\nJavaScript extraction is turned on; the generated file will be written to **src/js/breakpoints.js**, and it will be emitted as an ES\u202fmodule. CSS extraction is also enabled, producing **src/css/breakpoints.css** with the variables attached to the **:root** selector. Both custom media queries and custom CSS properties are used. The extraction options are configured to include media queries, minimum and maximum widths, while resolution\u2011based queries are omitted. Finally, Prettier formatting will follow the settings found in the **.prettierrc** configuration file.",
  "reference_json": {
    "drupal": {
      "breakpointsPath": "themes/custom/mytheme/config/breakpoints",
      "themeName": "mytheme"
    },
    "js": {
      "enabled": true,
      "path": "src/js/breakpoints.js",
      "type": "module"
    },
    "css": {
      "enabled": true,
      "path": "src/css/breakpoints.css",
      "element": ":root",
      "customMedia": true,
      "customProperty": true
    },
    "options": {
      "mediaQuery": true,
      "resolution": false,
      "minWidth": true,
      "maxWidth": true
    },
    "prettier": {
      "configPath": ".prettierrc"
    }
  }
